From: mscharged-port
Subject: Rollback: a replay answers that the sound its step prepared is prepared
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

A replayed frame starts, stops, pauses and resumes no sound
(MSCHARGED_AUDIO_ACTION, tweak patch 0031), and returns the value given:
false, for PrepareTrackedSound. NisPlayer::PrepareNisCue reads it, and
keeps the cinematic's cue (mPreparedNisCue, among what a rollback
restores) only when it is true. A rollback through the step that prepares
the end of the match's cinematic, some forty steps before its end, so left
no cue to start: StartNisCue started nothing, and the winners' celebration
played without its music and its voices, which are that one cue. The
sound the step's first run prepared stayed prepared, unheard.

In a replay, PrepareTrackedSound now answers as the step's first run did:
the sound it prepared is still the audio's, by its cue and context. The
other sound calls of a replay keep their value: no caller reads it.

A cue only a replay prepares (a step whose first run, on predicted
inputs, did not) is still not prepared.

diff --git a/src/Game/Audio/audio.cpp b/src/Game/Audio/audio.cpp
index 2fc9a62..e2985c7 100644
--- a/src/Game/Audio/audio.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Audio/audio.cpp
@@ -911,7 +911,14 @@ bool PrepareTrackedSound(int slotId, unsigned long cueId,
     void* context, bool resumable)
 {
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
-    MSCHARGED_AUDIO_ACTION(false);
+    // A replay prepares nothing, and answers as the step's first run did:
+    // the sound it prepared is still the audio's, by its cue and context.
+    // NisPlayer keeps a cinematic's cue only when this says it is prepared.
+    if (mscharged_rollback_resimulating())
+    {
+        return FindSoundHandle(cueId, context) != 0;
+    }
+    MSCHARGED_AUDIO_SCOPE();
 #endif
     XSoundHandle* handle = CreateSoundHandle(
         slotId, cueId, owner, debugName, context, false);
